# Eloquent & migrations

Inspect current schema, relations, indexes, and query patterns before changing anything. Prefer backward-compatible migrations. Never drop tables, columns, or data without explicit instruction.

Keep models, migrations, factories, and API contracts consistent. Destructive changes require explicit approval.

**Do:** `$fillable` (or the app's existing guard convention) for request-derived writes; eager-load relations you will iterate; anonymous migrations if that is already the app style.

**Don't:** `$guarded = []` plus `$request->all()`; `Schema::drop` in production paths without approval; `User::all()` then `$user->posts` in a loop (N+1).

```php
// Don't
Post::all()->each(fn ($post) => $post->author->name);

// Do
Post::query()->with('author')->paginate();
```

If schema changes are required, include: the migration file, a data-preservation strategy, rollback consideration, and deployment safety notes. Minimal migration size does not justify skipping safety.
